%N A069788 Number of tilings by lozenges of hexagon with sides n, n+1, n, n+1, n, n+1 and central triangle removed.
%D A069788 J. Propp, Enumeration of matchings: problems and progress, pp. 255-291 in L. J. Billera et al., eds, New Perspectives in Algebraic Combinatorics, Cambridge, 1999 (see Problem 1).
%H A069788 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A069788/b069788.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..53</a>
%H A069788 Harald A. Helfgott and Ira M. Gessel, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/1448">Tilings of Diamonds and Hexagons with Defects</a>, Electron. J. Combin., 6 (1999) (see Theorem 20).
%H A069788 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a069/A069788.java">Java program</a> (github)
%H A069788 James Propp, <a href="http://faculty.uml.edu/jpropp/update.pdf">Updated article</a>
%H A069788 James Propp, <a href="https://library.slmath.org/books/Book38/files/propp.pdf">Enumeration of Matchings: Problems and Progress</a>, in L. J. Billera et al. (eds.), New Perspectives in Algebraic Combinatorics, MSRI Publications, Vol. 38, Cambridge Univ. Press, 1999, pp. 255-291.
%F A069788 From _Seiichi Manyama_, Jul 28 2026: (Start)
%F A069788 For k >= 0,
%F A069788 a(2*k+1) = Product_{j=0..k} ((k+j+1)*(3*k-j+2))^(4*j+1) / (2^(2*k*(2*k+1)) * Product_{j=1..k}   (2*j+1)^(8*(k-j)+2)), and
%F A069788 a(2*k)   = Product_{j=1..k} ((k+j)*(3*k-j+1))^(4*j-1)   / (2^(2*k*(2*k-1)) * Product_{j=1..k-1} (2*j+1)^(8*(k-j)-2)). (End)
%o A069788 (PARI) a(n) = my(k=n\2); if(n%2, prod(j=0, k, ((k+j+1)*(3*k-j+2))^(4*j+1))/(2^(2*k*(2*k+1))*prod(j=1, k, (2*j+1)^(8*(k-j)+2))), prod(j=1, k, ((k+j)*(3*k-j+1))^(4*j-1))/(2^(2*k*(2*k-1))*prod(j=1, k-1, (2*j+1)^(8*(k-j)-2)))); \\ _Seiichi Manyama_, Jul 28 2026
